// PARKED — see ../README.md, "What is parked, and why".
//
// Zoo edge: LKMM -> x86-TSO (compilation). Runnable at last — the LKMM operand
// is ../../derived/lkmm.kat, generated by ../derive-lkmm.sh (see
// ../queries/strictly-weaker-SC-vs-LKMM.kat for why) — but not settled.
//
// The obstacle is event typing, not ordering. LKMM's derived relations carry no
// type restriction on their endpoints: acq-po is [ACQ];po and po-rel is
// po;[REL], where kater cannot tell that an LKMM release is a write and an
// acquire is a read, and the dependency relations are likewise untyped (IMM, by
// contrast, writes ppo as [R];(deps|rfi)+;[W]). TSO's ppo covers exactly the
// typed cases — [R];po and po;[W] — so the query is refuted on
//
//     [lkmm::Marked&ACQ] po [lkmm::Marked]
//
// Supplying the typing as premises does not discharge it: kater handles generic
// `a <= b` assumptions heuristically (manual §2.2.2, footnote 1), and of the
// forms tried, `assume [ACQ] <= [R]` and `assume po ; [REL] <= po ; [W]` are
// reported as "Ignoring unsupported assumption", while `assume [REL] ; [REL] <=
// [W]` is taken and does clear the po;[REL] counterexample — the ACQ half then
// still stands. Settling this means typing the endpoints in the LKMM rendering
// itself rather than assuming them, which is a change to the model file and not
// to the query.
//
// LKMM -> ARMv8 is refuted identically, on the same counterexample.
// LKMM -> POWER is vacuous against every Power rendering kater ships that is
// not itself refuted — see compilation-IMM-vs-POWER.kat for that.
// LKMM -> RVWMO is out of reach: kater ships no RISC-V model (dataset issue #3
// is the same gap on the memalloy side).
include "../../kat/tso.kat"
include "../../derived/lkmm.kat"

assume [ACQ] ; [ACQ] <= [R]
assume [REL] ; [REL] <= [W]
assume addr <= [R] ; addr
assume data <= [R] ; data ; [W]
assume ctrl <= [R] ; ctrl

assert lkmm::hb <= tso::tso+
